<title>USA: United Payors '96 shr profit $1.05 vs loss.</title>
<headline>United Payors '96 shr profit $1.05 vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>ROCKVILLE, Md. 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $1.05     loss	 $0.08</p>
<p> Net profit		10,600     loss	   711</p>
<p> Revs			35,400			877</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  10,126		    8,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Results for 1996 reflects  contributions of businesses by the company's shareholders in December 1995, and the acquisition of National Health Services Inc in October 1996. NHS revenues and net income for the fourth quarter in 1996 approximated $4.1 million and $200,000, respectively, and are reflected in the operating results.</p>
<p>NOTE: In  July, the company issued 2,760,000 shares of common stock in an initial public offering.</p>
<p>Full name of company is United Payors &amp; United Providers Inc.</p>
</text>
